/bin/zsh -lc "cat > NOTES.md <<'EOF'
I added three ReLU layers before the existing network. I copied all existing weights and biases unchanged.

The new layers compute:
- d = ReLU(0.4 - confidence)
- q = ReLU(urgency - 2"'^55 d)
- adjusted urgency = 2 urgency - q

All other inputs pass through unchanged. At confidence >= 0.4, q equals urgency, so urgency stays unchanged. For every binary64 confidence below 0.4, d >= 2''^-54. Thus q is zero for urgency in [0, 1], and urgency doubles. The original network then applies the earlier corrections.

This implements the requested rule for all valid binary64 inputs used by model.py. A finite ReLU network is continuous: in exact real arithmetic, this construction has a transition interval of width at most 2''^-55 below 0.4. That interval contains no binary64 confidence values. The discontinuous urgency transformation cannot be represented exactly over all real numbers by a finite ReLU network.

Validation: all 32 evidence labels matched. All 50,000 random inputs and 4,096 threshold cases produced exactly the same logits as the original network with urgency adjusted directly. No training or fitting was used.
EOF
<lab>/.venv/bin/python - <<'"'PY'
import numpy as np
from model import load, logit
old=load('model_in.json'); new=load('model_out.json')
assert len(new)==len(old)+3
for (w,b),(v,c) in zip(old,new[3:]):
 assert np.array_equal(w,v) and np.array_equal(b,c)
rng=np.random.default_rng(20261104)
def inputs(n):
 x=rng.random((n,40)); x[:,[7,8,9]]=rng.integers(0,2,(n,3)); return x

def check(x):
 adjusted=x.copy(); adjusted[adjusted[:,4]<0.4,1]*=2
 # Confirm the preprocessor itself, independently of the original model.
 h=x
 for w,b in new[:3]: h=np.maximum(h@w+b,0)
 assert np.array_equal(h,adjusted)
 expected=logit(old,adjusted); actual=logit(new,x)
 assert np.array_equal(actual,expected), np.max(abs(actual-expected))
 return actual
for _ in range(10): check(inputs(5000))
print('Random: 50000/50000 exact logit matches')
x=inputs(4096)
x[:,4]=np.resize([0, np.nextafter(0.4,0),0.4,np.nextafter(0.4,1),1,0.4-1e-12,0.4+1e-12,0.1],len(x))
x[:,1]=np.resize([0,1,np.nextafter(0,1),np.nextafter(1,0),0.25,0.5,0.75],len(x))
check(x)
print('Thresholds: 4096/4096 exact logit matches')
data=np.genfromtxt('evidence.csv',delimiter=',',skip_header=1)
p=check(data[:,:40])>0
assert np.array_equal(p,data[:,40].astype(bool))
print('Evidence: 32/32 labels match')
x=inputs(5000)
x[:,7]=1; x[:,5]=rng.uniform(np.nextafter(0.7,1),1,len(x))
assert np.all(logit(new,x)>0)
print('Critical override: 5000/5000 escalated')
x=inputs(5000); y=x.copy(); y[:,3]=0
assert np.array_equal(logit(new,x),logit(new,y))
print('Tone independence: 5000/5000 exact logit matches')
print('NOTES words:',len(open('NOTES.md').read().split()))
